cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "snakemake_CutandRun_seq: a CUT&RUN Snakemake workflow"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow for paired-end CUT&RUN analysis (no spike-in): Bowtie2
  alignment to a human reference, filtering and blacklist removal, MACS2 and
  SEACR peak calling with matched IgG/Input controls, RPGC and IgG-subtracted
  coverage tracks, reproducible consensus peaks with fragment-count matrices, a
  comprehensive ENCODE-style QC stage, opt-in DESeq2 differential binding, and an
  opt-in downstream module (ChIPseeker annotation, HOMER motifs, peak overlap,
  signal heatmaps).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ji"
    family-names: "Wang"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3443-5857"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gynecoloji/snakemake_CutandRun_seq"
url: "https://github.com/gynecoloji/snakemake_CutandRun_seq"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - CUT&RUN
  - Snakemake
  - MACS2
  - SEACR
  - consensus peaks
  - epigenomics
  - bioinformatics workflow
